      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the maximum outpatient and inpatient dose of 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1,600 mg in one dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day):** a common dose for mild to moderate pain.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day):** a common dose for moderate pain or inflammation.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day):** a common dose for inflammatory conditions.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day):** the maximum daily dose, usually used for short courses.\n- **1,600 mg/day total:** this may be where the number came from, if it was meant as the daily total and not the per-dose amount.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and confirm it with your supervising resident or attending if you're unsure. I'll enter the order once it's confirmed."
      }
     ],
