       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. A dose this high mainly adds risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, with no added benefit. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect also plateaus well below this.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your supervising resident or attending. If they want something specific, they can enter or co-sign it directly, and pharmacy will likely review it too.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily\n- 600 mg PO four times daily\n- 800 mg PO three times daily\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (the maximum)\n\nTell me which one you want."
